From 6cf2b143a71d7afaccd0b83689931c57215825ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xuxh1 <18172956238@163.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 07:48:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(hydro): take the lake evaporation deficit out of the
 routing storage (I-29)

DEF_LAKE_EVAP_ROUTING (default .false.). A lake patch gives no runoff when its evaporation exceeds its precipitation, and the land side books the difference (lake_deficit) as water put back into the patch with xerr set to zero, so that evaporation never leaves any store. With the key on, the grid-based routing gathers lake_deficit per unit catchment the way it gathers runoff and takes it out of the storage at the routing step, as far as the storage goes; the rest is owed and carried to later steps (restart field acc_ldef_uc). The C-44 floodplain evaporation then leaves out the flooded area the lake patches cover, which they already evaporate. A yearly log line gives the lake patch deficit, the part that reached a unit catchment, the part taken from storage and what is still owed. Closed with the Dynamic Lake, which sets no deficit. With the key off every existing statement is unchanged.

---
 main/HYDRO/MOD_Grid_RiverLakeFlow.F90     | 139 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 main/HYDRO/MOD_Grid_RiverLakeTimeVars.F90 |  42 ++++++-
 share/MOD_Namelist.F90                    |  16 +++
 3 files changed, 194 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/main/HYDRO/MOD_Grid_RiverLakeFlow.F90 b/main/HYDRO/MOD_Grid_RiverLakeFlow.F90
